body:
Word got back to us. You've been moving product for {{enemy}}.

We don't forget who feeds our enemies. Think about that.

- {{org}}

Somebody saw you with {{enemy}}. That's not the company we keep.

Don't make a habit of it.

- {{org}}

You did business with {{enemy}}. We know.

Every crate you hand them costs you with us.

- {{org}}

Heard you've been friendly with {{enemy}} lately.

Their friends don't get our prices. Your call.

- {{org}}

You've made yourself useful lately. We still remember, but the bosses agreed to stop lowballing you quite so hard.

Keep going.

- {{org}}

Product keeps arriving and nobody's had to chase you.

That buys you a little slack. A little.

- {{org}}

You're less of a problem than you were. That's an update, not a compliment.

Check the rates.

- {{org}}

The bosses noticed you showing up. Rates moved a hair in your favor.

Don't waste it.

- {{org}}

Whatever was between us, consider it settled.

You bring product, we pay fair. Don't complicate it.

- {{org}}

The bosses talked. You're square with us. Normal rates, no grudges.

What you build from here is on you.

- {{org}}

Clean slate as of today.

You get the same deal as anybody else. Earn better if you want it.

- {{org}}

Nobody's holding anything against you anymore.

That's worth more than the rate change. Use it.

- {{org}}

You've been steady, and steady is rare in this line of work.

The bosses want you close. You'll see it in the numbers.

- {{org}}

We like how you move. Quiet, reliable, no drama.

People like that get paid better here. Check the rates.

- {{org}}

Your name came up in a good way for once.

The rates went up with it.

- {{org}}

You keep showing up, and the product keeps being what you said it was.

That's worth money. It's in your rates now.

- {{org}}

There aren't many people we'd call untouchable. As of today you're one of them.

Best rates we pay anybody. Don't make us regret it.

- {{org}}

Your name came up at the table last night. Nobody had a bad word.

Whatever you're selling, we're buying first, at the best price you'll find.

- {{org}}

You're one of ours now. Top dollar, no questions.

It also means we expect you to act like it.

- {{org}}

Short list. You're on it.

Nobody gets better numbers out of us than you do.

- {{org}}

Whatever trust there was is gone.

We'll still take your product. At scrap prices. Don't expect a welcome.

- {{org}}

The bosses are through with you.

Bottom dollar until you make things right, if that's even possible.

- {{org}}

You burned it. All of it.

Come by if you want, but you'll get what we give anyone we don't trust.

- {{org}}

You know how you got here.

The rates are at the floor. So is our patience.

- {{org}}

You're on thin ice.

The rates just got worse. They'll keep getting worse if this continues.

- {{org}}

Choices have prices. Yours just cost you ours.

Check the rates and think about where this is heading.

- {{org}}

The bosses are asking questions about you. That's never good.

You get less from us until they stop.

- {{org}}

We took a step back from you today.

One more and you're nobody to us.

- {{org}}

Whatever goodwill you'd built, you've spent some of it.

Back to treating you like anyone else off the street.

- {{org}}

The special treatment is over.

Standard rates from here. Earn better ones back if you care to.

- {{org}}

We stopped doing you favors as of today.

Nothing personal. You just stopped earning them.

- {{org}}

You were top of our list. Were.

The bosses saw things they didn't like and the rates moved to match.

- {{org}}

Consider this a friendly warning, since you've earned that much.

You're slipping. Don't slip further.

- {{org}}

Something changed with you, and it wasn't for the better.

Your numbers changed with it.

- {{org}}

We had you high. Not that high anymore.

Get back to how you were.

- {{org}}

Our man handed you a package. It goes to {{location}}, you got {{minutes}} minutes.

Don't open it. Don't be late. Don't get followed.

- {{org}}

You've got the package. {{location}}, {{minutes}} minutes.

Leave it and walk like you were never there.

- {{org}}

Simple job. The package goes to {{location}}.

You have {{minutes}} minutes before we start assuming the worst.

- {{org}}

Package to {{location}}. {{minutes}} minutes on the clock.

Map's below. Don't make us send someone after it.

- {{org}}

Someone's been a problem for us. He's around {{location}} right now.

Make him stop being a problem inside {{minutes}} minutes. Don't get seen.

- {{org}}

There's a guy at {{location}} nobody will miss.

{{minutes}} minutes before he moves on. We'll remember this one.

- {{org}}

A rat's sitting at {{location}}.

Handle him however you like. Just make it inside {{minutes}} minutes.

- {{org}}

{{location}}. Our problem is standing right there.

{{minutes}} minutes. Map's below.

- {{org}}

There's a car at {{location}} that needs to stop existing.

Torch it, wreck it, drive it off a cliff. {{minutes}} minutes.

- {{org}}

A car at {{location}} is a loose end.

Make it scrap inside {{minutes}} minutes and we're square.

- {{org}}

Somebody left their ride at {{location}}.

Be a shame if something happened to it in the next {{minutes}} minutes.

- {{org}}

{{location}}. One vehicle. {{minutes}} minutes.

We don't care how. Map's below.

- {{org}}

Heard it went clean.

The bosses noticed. You'll see it in how we treat you.

- {{org}}

Job's done and nobody's asking questions.

Exactly how we like it. We owe you one.

- {{org}}

Word came back. Good work.

Keep this up and doors start opening.

- {{org}}

That's handled. No mess, no names.

You're worth more to us today than you were yesterday.

- {{org}}

That was our property you touched, doing {{rival}}'s dirty work.

We don't forget faces. Watch yourself.

- {{org}}

You did a job on us for {{rival}} and figured nobody would connect it.

We did. Every door of ours just got heavier.

- {{org}}

You hurt us to please {{rival}}. Fine.

Choices like that have a price, and we keep the ledger.

- {{org}}

{{rival}} pointed and you moved. On us.

Remember that the next time you need something from us.

- {{org}}

The job didn't get done.

We don't hand out chances like that twice in a row. Remember whose time you wasted.

- {{org}}

We asked for one thing. It's still not done, and now it's too late.

The bosses will remember.

- {{org}}

You said yes and then nothing happened.

That costs you with us.

- {{org}}

The deadline came and went.

Next time we give the work to someone who finishes it.

- {{org}}
